{"name":"Red Fang","hex":"#c54831","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"fang","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, pointed canine tooth used for biting and tearing flesh. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Synonym of mandible, the long mouthpart of insects and other invertebrates."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike or attack with the fangs.","To enable to catch or tear; to furnish with fangs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fang"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Fang","blocks":[{"text":"Red Fang is an American rock band from Portland, Oregon, formed in 2005. It is composed of guitarist and vocalist Bryan Giles, bassist and vocalist Aaron Beam, guitarist David Sullivan and drummer John Sherman. The band has released five albums: Red Fang (2009), Murder the Mountains (2011), Whales and Leeches (2013), Only Ghosts (2016) and Arrows (2021)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Red_Fang-13.jpg/330px-Red_Fang-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Fang"},{"title":"Red Fang (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Fang is the first album by American stoner metal band Red Fang, released in 2009 on the Sargent House record label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/Red_Fang-Red_Fang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Fang_(album)"},{"title":"Fang","blocks":[{"text":"A fang is a long, pointed tooth. In mammals, a fang is a modified maxillary tooth, used for biting and tearing flesh. In snakes, it is a specialized tooth that is associated with a venom gland. Spiders also have external fangs, which are part of the chelicerae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Fangs_01_rfc1036.jpg/330px-Fangs_01_rfc1036.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fang"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Red_Fang_-_Wacken_Open_Air_-_160805LEOKR004381510000.jpg/500px-Red_Fang_-_Wacken_Open_Air_-_160805LEOKR004381510000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Red_Fang_-_Wacken_Open_Air_-_160805LEOKR004381510000.jpg/1280px-Red_Fang_-_Wacken_Open_Air_-_160805LEOKR004381510000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Red_Fang_-_Wacken_Open_Air_-_160805L